New: pocket mode (experimental).

A Bluetooth headset carries a microphone or music, never both, so holding it open for a whole ride drops the group and any music to telephone bandwidth. Pocket mode takes it only while you are talking.

Turn it on in Settings and slide the control at the bottom of the screen: it locks the screen, three taps on the phone — through a jacket — open the microphone, and a silence hands it back.

Off by default; tap detection is not yet measured on the road.
